-- HALO: restore public.profiles.address, so 0024's privacy functions run.
--
-- Run once in the Supabase SQL editor. Safe to re-run. One ADD COLUMN IF NOT
-- EXISTS with no default: a metadata-only change, no table rewrite.
--
-- WHY. 0024 (privacy) reads and clears profiles.address in
-- privacy_fingerprint, the inspect counts and clear all, as the reconstructed
-- schema (docs/backend/trial-schema-0001-0014.sql) has it. The production
-- table has no such column (found 2026-10-25 by the release isolation test:
-- `column profiles.address does not exist`). PL/pgSQL resolves columns only
-- when a statement runs, so 0024 applied cleanly but every call that touches
-- the profile row fails: Settings, Clear all app records, and the `home` and
-- `preferences` export groups answer 500.
--
-- WHAT. The column is added empty and stays empty: nothing in HALO writes it
-- (a privacy decision: the home is kept as a rounded point, never an
-- address). It exists only so 0024 runs as written and tested. 0015's revoke
-- covers it (no client writes), and 0003's select-own policy lets a household
-- read only its own row.

alter table public.profiles add column if not exists address text;

